A positive temperature coefficient means that the resistance (and the resistivity) of the metal rises when the temperature rises: $R=R_0(1+\alpha\theta)$ with $\alpha>0$. The same statement read in the opposite direction says that the resistance and the resistivity fall when the temperature falls. Hence:

- **A** (resistivity decreases when the temperature decreases) is true;
- **B** (resistance increases when the temperature increases) is true;
- **C** and **D** state the opposite behaviour (the behaviour of a thermistor, not of a metal) and are false.

Options A and B are both correct statements of the same fact, so the question has two correct options and no single key; no letter is designated.

